load @term/seed/code/structure/set
  find set

# A state: a complete description of a system at one moment, a point in the space of all the system's possibilities. A
# cell of the substrate is in a state (one of its ternary tones), and the whole mesh is in a state (the tones of all its
# cells), which the two-step rule advances each beat. In quantum mechanics a state is a vector in a Hilbert space. The
# form carries the set of possible states.
form state
  link space, like set
